{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Customer Profiling"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about customer profiling."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.  Build the IT system prototype, starting from the analysis of the functional characteristics of the system regarding user-friendliness, functionality and user experience, supported in software applied following design protocols."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about customer profile creation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think about other possible ways to collect customer's profile information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a presentation to a partner explaining your ideas. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about customer profile creation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design new ways to collect costumer information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a presentation about it to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I receive feedback on my presentation."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "be familiar with "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have knowledge or training in some field."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are you familiar with this kind of systems?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "improve "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something better or to enhance it."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Remember that having customer profiles enables us to improve contact with them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "powerful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very strong, capable or mighty."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We have got some powerful online channels to gather information."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sort "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "type or kind of something."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you got any sort of example I can look at?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "social networks "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "websites in which people can interact with one another."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "And now I'm also getting the amount of times this person has interacted with us on the phone and social networks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gap"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "blank space, hole or space to complete."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm creating the profile by completing the gaps on the customer's profile."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Have Got (Review)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>Have got</strong> &nbsp;means the same as <strong>have</strong>, but it is more informal. Use it when you want to express that something belongs to you, or to talk about the characteristics that something has.&nbsp;</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Though I think I've got to see if this one is different from the ones I used in my previous job."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you got any sort of example I can look at?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>In order to use <strong>have got</strong>, you need to take into account that the verb <strong>have</strong> changes depending on the person it follows:</p> <p>I have</p> <p>You have</p> <p><strong>He has</strong></p> <p><strong>She has</strong></p> <p><strong>It has</strong></p> <p>We have</p> <p>They have</p> <p>After <strong><i>have</i></strong>, you use <strong><i>got</i></strong>, which doesn&rsquo;t change. You can use <strong><i>have</i> <i>got</i> to </strong>ask questions, for affirmative and negative sentences.</p> <p>Examples:</p> <ul> <li><strong><i>Have </i></strong><i>you <strong>got </strong>the file with the customer profile I asked you for?</i></li> <li><i>Yes, I <strong>have</strong> <strong>got</strong> it now!</i></li> <li><i>No, I <strong>haven&rsquo;t</strong> <strong>got</strong> it yet.</i></li> </ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Customer Vs. Client"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Sometimes, business owners use these terms that look like synonyms to refer to people who make business deals with them. However, they are slightly different. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<p align=\"justify\">Remember that having customer profiles enables us to improve contact with them.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<p align=\"justify\">We can also keep track of their interaction with our organization so that we can provide them with the products or services they need.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <p align=\"justify\">People often use these two terms interchangeably, but the difference remains on what the person (client or customer) needs. Take a look at the following explanation: </br></br>   <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\"> Client </span></div> </br></br>  Clients are the people who need and pay for the services of a professional in any particular field. For example: private teachers, lawyers, accountants and so on. </br></br>   <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\"> Customer </span></div></br></br>  On the other hand, customers are the people who buy things from businesses. Not necessarily from a person or group of people like clients would.  </br></br></p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n4le02ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>David: </strong>Well, Paul, in today&rsquo;s training you&rsquo;ll learn how to create a customer profile. Are you familiar with this kind of systems?</p>\n<p><strong>Paula: </strong>Yes. Though I think I&rsquo;ve got to see if this one is different from the ones I used in my previous job.</p>\n<p><strong>David</strong>: All right. First of all. Remember that having customer profiles enables us to improve contact with them. We can also keep track of their interaction with our organization so we can provide them with the products or services they need, and also reach a broader audience.</p>"}, {"time": "32000", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Paula</strong>: Noted. How does your system work?</p>\n<p><strong>David</strong>: We have got some powerful online channels to gather information, like our own website, our email accounts, and our social media pages. The system puts that information together and places it on our servers. Then you can retrieve it by typing the customer&rsquo;s name or email in the platform. Then, all the information will be provided to you automatically.</p>\n<p><strong>Paula</strong>: Well, have you got any sort of example I can look at?</p>\n<p><strong>David</strong>: Sure. Let&rsquo;s create a profile, I&rsquo;m going to use this training tools we have to show you how it works. The client&rsquo;s name is John Doe.</p>"}, {"time": "75000", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Paula</strong>: Okay. So, I&rsquo;m typing it here. It&rsquo;s blank!</p>\n<p><strong>David</strong>: Some extra information will appear gradually, so you need to update it on the system.</p>\n<p><strong>Paula</strong>: I can see it now. We&rsquo;ve got the person&rsquo;s email and the phone number, but we haven&rsquo;t got his address. It says that this customer always shops online. And now, I&rsquo;m also getting the amount of times this person has interacted with us on the phone and on social networks. I&rsquo;m creating the profile by completing the gaps on the customer&rsquo;s profile.</p>\n<p><strong>David</strong>: You see? It was very difficult before, but now it&rsquo;s a breeze!</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n4le02ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain how to create a customer profile."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about different tools related to online channels."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can create a cus